And he made a nice living. Hard-- he worked very hard, my father worked hard. And my three oldest brothers helped already, worked with him. Yeah. And when my sister was married-- not-- not-- not the early when she-- I mean, my sister was married, and they had a husband and a child.

And a brother of mine was married, but this brother still worked with my father and the two other brothers. He taught them the-- they-- they-- they-- what-- how to-- how to do what he was doing.

And they liked it, and he was paying them like he was paying the strangers. But they were good children. And what else should I tell you? I was-- I don't know how to go with the age.

[LAUGHS]

Well, we all finished only grade schools, up to the-- not the youngest, because the youngest didn't go to school yet. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS] My father was sending out the goods, and then they gave him checks.

