And she was one of our people. And after she let go, I, I was beaten up. And we're still, we're licking the snow. Bread, nobody was hungry. I was thinking something. How comes we don't want to eat? Nobody was hungry.

Everybody, it was about two weeks already, we were driving around. Nobody was hungry, only thirsty. One day I say, after she beat me up, we're sitting together, a bunch of people. I says, I'm jumping off the train. I'm not going any further.

