And he talks to him. And the man doesn't talk to me. He-- let's go. [SPEAKING GERMAN]. Well, what should I do? I could walk already. Not walk good, but I could schlep myself.

The ice was running down me and everything. He had a car down there. He had a car down, down, where from the thing.

Took me to a car. And he brought me into a place. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS] And opened the door. And there is a, a loft like, a loft with about 24 people, Gestapo, Gestapo clothing, and young men sitting with their back to me, but they all have the uniforms.

And he starts talking loud. And everybody moves around in their chair, like this, and looks at me. [SPEAKING GERMAN]. he said, [GERMAN], and he told him what the guy told him, and that, that I came walking in.

