He says, take everything off. Take all your clothes off. I said, oh nein, [GERMAN SPEECH]. I wouldn't do that.

[GERMAN SPEECH]! What's wrong with you? I said, nothing is wrong with me. I wouldn't undress in-- why should I undress in front of you?

What do you want to do? I said, pull up my sleeves. And I want to wash my face. And then I've seen my face, how it was cracked up, black and red, and-- oh, nein. [GERMAN SPEECH].

Nein. He doesn't let me do this. I said, [GERMAN SPEECH], I would not undress in front of you.

[GERMAN SPEECH] when you undress? What-- what did I do to you? What will I do to you if you undress?

I don't know. I don't want to undress. I want to undress. I want to wash my face, rinse my hands and wash my face.

