[PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS]

[LAUGHS] I-- should I tell you another story? The gypsies, she had to go to bathroom-- excuse me. I have to tell you. So she spread her legs in the middle of the street. There's roughage everywhere.

And they still wanted me to go shopping with them-- shopping-- selling, selling, selling. What they-- they want me for? I didn't know.

I was going for a while, and then I said, I don't want to go anymore. Do whatever you want. I don't want to go anymore.

OK. I don't have to catch. I don't have to do-- I-- I-- I have to be with them. Why? It's better this way. [PAUSES FOR 4 SECONDS] It was no good. I didn't like it.

One day, it was-- time was flying up, right? Flying away.

