EK: Of '44 I think, right? Yes? '44. [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] Yeah. The Russians came flying one day. And they killed a horse. And they flew away-- Russians air-- airplane-- aeroplanes. They killed a horse and flew away.

Killed the horse-- so that's where all gypsies stay in the area. Everybody went out, and they were cutting it up. And they made horse hamburgers. And I ate the horse hamburger, and it was good. [LAUGHS] I was hungry.

I didn't have enough that-- that piece of chicken they gave me. I don't know. They took off here, they took off there. It wasn't enough.

Anyway, in between, when I was hungry, I decided that I'm gonna-- they had eggs-- not raw-- yeah, raw eggs-- raw-- raw eggs. They had 'em between windows. And they also had a-- a speck. You know what speck is? A speck. Fat-- pig fat-- pig's fat-- pig's fat? Speck is-- speck is from pigs, right? I don't know.

Fat in-- in jars. They had fat. They let it out from something. They had eggs. [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] And they had flower. Between the windows there were-- there were little flowers planted there to look nice.

And when they put an egg there-- I seen they put in eggs-- so one day I said, why should I be so hungry? They are fat. They're heavy. They look good. They eat good, and I'm dying. I'm hungry.

I took a-- a spoon of fat, a fresh egg, two spoons of flour, into a dish. I mixed it up, and I ate it up. And I felt so good after it. I wasn't hungry. And then the chicken on top, I was fine.

So I stole something from them already. But they wouldn't know. They didn't know.

And what else? And then, yeah. After the aeroplane came, right-- I said the hamburgers. Then they-- everybody was talking that the Russians are coming. The Russians are coming. The Russians are coming. The Russians are coming.

[PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS]

